{title: Swallowed Up in Victory}
{subtitle: 1 Corinthians 15:51–57; Matthew 28:5–7; 1 Corinthians 15:12–22}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Cm7] | [Cm7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]The women came at sunrise with their spices and their tears
[Cm7]An angel met them at the tomb and spoke against their fears
He is [Ab]not here; he has ri[Eb/G]sen, just as he [Eb]said
Come and see the [Bb]place where he lay
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Death has been swallowed up in victory
Where, [Cm]O death, is your victory?
Where, O [Abmaj7]death, is your sting?
Thanks be to God, who gives us [Eb]the victory
Through our [Bb]Lord Jesus [Eb]Christ
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If Christ had not been raised, our hope would be an empty word
[Ebmaj7/D]We would [Cm7]still be in our sins, the saddest people on the earth
But in [Abmaj7]fact Christ has been raised from the dead
The firstfruits [Eb]of those who have fallen [Bb]as[Eb]leep
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Death has been swallowed up in victory
[Bb/D]Where, [Cm]O death, is your victory?
[Cm7/Bb]Where, O [Abmaj7]death, is your sting?
Thanks be to God, who gives us [Eb]the victory
Through our [Bb]Lord Jesus [Eb]Christ
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
In [Abmaj7]an instant, in the blink of [Bb]an eye, at the last trumpet
The [Cm]trumpet will sound, and the dead will [Gm]be raised imperishab[Abmaj7]le
And we will be [Eb]changed
And we will [Ebmaj7/D]be [Cm]changed
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Death has been swallowed up in victory
[Ebmaj7/D]Where, [Cm]O death, is your victory?
[Cm7/Bb]Where, O [Abmaj7]death, is your sting?
Thanks be to God, who gives us [Eb]the victory
Through our [Bb]Lord Jesus [Eb]Christ
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
He [Ebmaj7/D]is not [Abmaj7]here; he has risen
Thanks be to [Eb]God
{end_of_verse}
